(Regression test: a failed float cast sets _last_error, but a later
successful float cast clears it so a subsequent On error does not fire.
The texts are read at run time: a literal that is not a number is refused
by the compiler.)

a text called word is "not a float".
a text called other is "also bad".
a text called digits is "3.14".
A float called bad is word as a float.
On error print "first".

A float called bad2 is other as a float.
A float called good is digits as a float.
On error print "second".
Print bad.
Print good.
